      "narrative": "Maricopa County’s September residential market softened: the median sales price fell 2% year over year to $500,000, while the average sales price rose 1.2% to $686,802.[1] Inventory increased 6.4% to 15,422 homes, equivalent to 3.9 months of supply versus 3.7 months a year earlier.[1] Buyer activity weakened sharply, with pending sales down 39.3%, while closed sales fell 5.3% and new listings declined 1.2%; sellers received 98.1% of asking price.[1] Affordability pressure, including mortgage rates and home prices, was cited as delaying the seasonal market pickup, while year-to-date sales remained above 2025 levels.[1]",
