      "narrative": "Pinal County’s median sale price was $371,514, down 1.1% from a year earlier and 2.2% from the prior month.[1] Inventory stood at 2,657 homes for sale, with 3.5 months of supply and 77 days on market, indicating more choice and greater negotiating room for buyers than in a tight seller’s market.[1] Local demand is supported by manufacturing and semiconductor-related investment, including Lucid Motors, Kohler, Abbott Nutrition, Hexcel, and other companies, while Maricopa also draws commuters to Chandler and Tempe employment centers.[3][8] Population growth in Casa Grande and Maricopa, new industrial development along the I-10 and Union Pacific corridor, and continued construction are notable local drivers, although water-supply constraints remain a concern.[8][9]",
