      "narrative": "Pima County’s median sale price reached $371,500 in September 2026, up 3.1% from a year earlier.[3] Inventory was building into October, while the county recorded 991 closings, down 8.3% year over year.[3] Buyer leverage increased: 44% of sellers reduced their price before closing, homes went under contract in a median 36 days, and sellers received 98% of final list price.[3] The county’s housing affordability crisis remains a notable local constraint, while a proposed American Battery Factory project remains stalled and has not become a major employer.[2]",
